WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.902
-You play Frank Sheeran...
-Yeah.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.771
-...who they called
"The Irishman."

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:07.507
And you just -- Man,
you go for it in this movie.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:10.042
A lot of people get hurt
because of you.

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:14.113
But...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:18.350
But, somehow, you make me love
you and feel for you.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.687
And you're kind of a middleman.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:24.290
You're kind of stuck in a lot of
situations where you're like,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.025
"Why am I stuck in
the middle of this?

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.327
But I'll do it."

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.295
And I just --
You made me feel for you.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.898
I went up and down, roller
coaster, and at the end,

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.234
there wasn't a dry eye in the
movie theater where I saw it.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.969
Did an amazing thing
and they did a technology

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:39.138
that I'd never seen before --

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:41.240
maybe a little bit in
"Avengers,"

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.575
but it wasn't like this.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:46.513
They reversed-aged you.
-Yes. Yeah.

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:48.280
-How?

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.386
-Well, it took
a lot of work to do.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.754
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.754 --> 00:00:58.224
I mean, I'm happy, 'cause maybe
it will extend my career

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.458
another 30 years.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:01.194
-Yeah. You're gonna be in movies
for the rest of --

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.262
Yeah, even past your life, yeah.

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:04.597
But did they put --
Did you have, like,

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.032
dots all over your face
when you're acting?

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.200
-We had slight dots.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.503
They didn't want it
to get in our way,

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.739
and Marty didn't want that.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.508
I did one other things once,
and we had all kinds of stuff,

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:18.711
but this they did
very subtly and so on.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:22.014
So, they had references
for little kinds of cameras

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:26.085
taking pictures and a special
camera photographing us.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:29.421
-I mean, most of the movie,
you're young.

00:01:29.421 --> 00:01:32.392
-Yeah, a lot of it -- Yeah.
And then --

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:35.061
-Did they change
your voice, as well?

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.195
-No, they didn't.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:37.896
I mean, I changed it
more toward the end.

00:01:37.896 --> 00:01:41.000
-Of course you changed it.
I love it. Yes! Yes!

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.102
Yeah! You're like, "Yeah, I'm
gonna show you how to do it."

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:46.772
Yeah. "Watch out, computers."
Yeah, I know what to do. Yeah."

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:49.075
Let me just show you this so
people can see what I'm talking
about.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:53.612
Here's you as Frank in your 20s.
This is in World War II.

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:56.816
It's not just a photo.
This is a scene.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:02:03.723
And it's an amazing scene.
Here's you as Frank in your 40s.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:08.828
Yeah. And here's you
in your 60s.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:13.466
And then here's you in your 80s.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:16.436
I mean, it's unbelievable
what you do.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:20.440
The nuances to each decade --
I'm telling you --

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.041
you are such a great actor.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.910
I don't know if you know that.
-Oh, thanks.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.980
-But, man, oh, man.
What a story.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.316
I mean, is there anything
that you can tell people

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.951
about this movie
that if they go like,

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.519
"Oh, this is gonna be another
'Goodfellas.'"

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.255
It's not really.
-No, it's not.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:38.925
It was a -- The thing --
It's a very simple story.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:42.628
It's about loyalty
and a guy stuck in the middle

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:47.700
of two people who totally --
I mean, he had to make a choice.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.370
It was a matter of
survival, actually, for him

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.706
to make the choice that he did.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.008
Not to give it away.
-Oh, yeah, of course. Yeah.

00:02:56.008 --> 00:02:58.410
-So, it's that simple.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:02.248
-It's about family, too, and
it's about life and death and --

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.549
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:06.986
And Al Pacino is amazing as
Jimmy Hoffa.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.454
Everybody's great.
Ray Romano is great.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.688
-Ray is great.

00:03:09.688 --> 00:03:12.458
-It's just -- I just loved
every single thing.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:15.195
Even down to the detail, by
the way, of, like --

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:17.897
I don't know if it's CGI,
if it's real,

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:22.135
like, but Scorsese has --
The TV stand that it was on

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.303
in the '70s had these brass legs

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:26.239
with these white,
like, Lucite wheels.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.340
-Yeah.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.574
-I had that when
I was growing up.

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:30.008
I'm like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:03:30.008 --> 00:03:32.912
Like, I love a movie
that has that much detail.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.048
You guys are gonna flip out.

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:37.049
You have a special treat
for us tonight.

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:40.185
We're gonna debut the trailer,
a brand-new trailer.

00:03:40.185 --> 00:03:43.022
-Okay.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:46.225
-Here is "The Irishman,"
Robert De Niro.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:48.027
Take a look.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:52.465
-I'm here to defend you,
so you ever show up late?

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:55.301
-No.
-Do you drink on the job?

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.004
-No.
-You ever hit anybody?

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.572
-I don't think so.
-Alright then.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:03.176
We don't have
nothing to worry about.

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.944
-A friend of ours is having
a little trouble,

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.245
a friend at the top.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.314
-He's got a gun!

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:11.750
-Always charge a guy with a gun.
With a knife, you run.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.386
-Big business
and the government.

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.254
-We're going to war
with these people.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:18.057
-Things have gotten out of hand
with our friend.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:23.763
-I know things
they don't know I know.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:29.868
-It's gonna happen.
Either way, he's going.

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:32.939
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Rated R.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:36.809
-Let me just say "wow."
Look at everybody say, "Wow."

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:40.246
That's what I'm talking about.
Robert De Niro, everybody.

